    "text": "Gavrinis is a Breton mythological site. The name is also written Gavr'inis. An island sits in a small harbor off the coast of Morbihan in southern Brittany. The island holds a richly engraved ritual chamber. This chamber far predates the Celts. Its spiral iconography links it to Ireland's Brú na Bóinne. Deep incised carvings decorate more than twenty enormous granite uprights. Its megalithic rock architecture resembles Britain's Stonehenge. The purpose is unknown. Such monuments often line up with an astronomical point. Gavrinis points precisely to the winter solstice sunrise.",
